title: War Effort
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: potus_affairs, cabinet
view-if: spain_war = 1 and war_stage < 4 and war_room_timer <= 0
card-image: img/CUBA.png
on-arrival: war_room_timer += 1;

= Prosecuting the War

With Congress and the President now committed to war, attention turns from speeches to strategy. Spain may be weakened by the ongoing Third Carlist War and the chaos of the Cantonal Rebellion, but even a distracted empire will not surrender its richest colony without a fight. Victory will require ships to command the sea, soldiers willing to storm hostile shores, and the resolve to sustain a campaign fought hundreds of miles from home.

[? if invasion_force_strength >= 1 : Our invasion force now numbers [+ invasion_force_strength +] thousand men and continues to grow as volunteers and regulars assemble in Southern ports. ?]
[? if cuban_blockade_strength >= 1 : The blockade around Cuba tightens with each passing week, placing increasing pressure on Spanish supply lines and commerce. ?]
[? if mambise_strength >= 1 : Armed with American weapons and supplies, the Mambise rebels have grown into a formidable guerrilla force, tying down Spanish garrisons across much of the island. ?]

- @mobilize_invasion_force: Mobilize an invasion force.
- @enforce_blockade: Enforce a blockade of Cuba.
- @smuggle_arms_mambises: Smuggle arms to the Mambise rebels.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@mobilize_invasion_force
subtitle: -2 budget.
choose-if: budget >= 2
view-if: invasion_force_strength < 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 2: Not enough budget. ?]
on-arrival: {! 
    Q.budget -= 2;
    Q.invasion_force_strength = (Q.army_strength * 0.4) + (Q.South_army_strength * 0.25);
    Q.army_strength *= 0.6;
    Q.South_army_strength *= 0.75
    Q.PoliticalCostPenalty += 2;
    Q.radical_strength += 2;
    Q.conservative_dissent += 2;
    Q.middle_class_dem += 1;
!}

Recruitment offices fill with volunteers while regular army regiments receive orders to concentrate along the Atlantic coast. Steamships are requisitioned, supply depots established, and military camps spring up from Virginia to Florida in preparation for an expedition unlike any the Republic has attempted. <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> hail the mobilization as the beginning of Cuba's liberation, while <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservatives**</span> warn that another costly foreign war may squander the peace so recently won. The nation's middle class, still haunted by the losses of the Civil War, watches the growing columns of marching men with quiet apprehension.

@enforce_blockade
subtitle: -1 budget. (Requires sizeable naval strength)
choose-if: budget >= 1 and navy_strength >= 200
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 1: Not enough budget. ?][? if navy_strength < 200: The Navy isn't strong enough to hold a blockade line. ?]
on-arrival: {! 
    Q.budget -= 1;
    Q.cuban_blockade_strength += 15;
    Q.spain_relation -= 3;
    Q.radical_strength += 1;
    Q.middle_class_rep += 1;
    if (Q.war_stage == 0)
    {
        Q.war_stage = 1;
    }
!}

Squadrons of American warships take up station off Havana, Cienfuegos, and Santiago, intercepting merchant vessels and sealing Cuba's principal ports. Every ship turned away weakens Spain's ability to reinforce or resupply the island, forcing its commanders to rely on dwindling local stockpiles. Madrid denounces the blockade as an act of piracy, but with the Carlist War and Cantonal Revolt consuming men, money, and political attention at home, Spain can spare little to challenge American naval superiority.

@smuggle_arms_mambises
subtitle: -0.5 budget. (Requires moderate naval strength)
choose-if: budget >= 0.5 and navy_strength >= 80
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 0.5: Not enough budget. ?][? if navy_strength < 80: We lack the ships to run the arms safely. ?]
on-arrival: {! 
    Q.budget -= 0.5;
    Q.mambise_strength += 12;
    Q.spain_relation -= 2;
    Q.radical_strength += 2;
    Q.freedmen_rep += 1;
!}

Under cover of darkness, fast steamers and blockade-runners ferry rifles, ammunition, medicine, and volunteers to the Mambise insurgents operating throughout Oriente and Camagüey. Every successful landing strengthens the Cuban resistance and forces Spain to divert valuable troops away from the coast and into an increasingly frustrating guerrilla campaign. Each crate of rifles delivered to the rebels is one fewer Spanish battalion available to oppose an eventual American landing.